## 🐙 Automatic Git & GitHub Pipeline

After executing and self-verifying a set of components or milestone tasks:

1. Stage all created and modified files (`git add .`).
2. Create a clean commit using **Conventional Commits** (e.g., `feat(physics): implement FAO-56 Penman-Monteith engine`, `docs: update system architecture`).
3. Push changes directly to the remote repository (`git push`).

---

## 🎯 Project Core Vision & Architecture

- **UX** — No-Form UX via dynamic 3D Canvas (`@react-three/fiber`, Three.js, Zustand) with interactive TransformControls/Gizmos.
- **Physics** — Real-time thermodynamic and biological calculation core strictly adhering to FAO standards (FAO-56 Penman-Monteith, FAO CLIMWAT, HWSD).
- **Multi-AI Gateway** — Decoupled AI provider layer (`backend/app/ai/`) supporting OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, and local Ollama models.
- **Database & Security** — Modular Supabase integration (PostgreSQL) with Row Level Security (RLS).
- **License** — Protective source-available license (BUSL-1.1).

---

